# Pass one of two: rank every opening move, and only that.
#
# The root is searched at MultiPV 36 -- every legal opening in every mode -- so
# that each one becomes an edge and therefore a position the book can expand.
# 23 was "every legal opening" while the only two modes shared a starting
# position; Intransitive opens from two diagonal wedges of ten pieces and has
# 36, so 23 there silently left the last thirteen openings with no edge, no
# node, and therefore no book at all if the opponent played one of them. A mode
# with fewer legal openings than this simply ranks all it has. Its own scores barely matter: as soon as a child is analyzed, the
# child's value replaces the estimate that reached it. So the root gets only
# enough budget to rank moves, and the real budget goes to the positions they
# reach, where twelve threads can work at once instead of one.
#
# The ply-1 margin is deliberately wide. A survey is supposed to look at every
# opening, including the ones it expects to refute.
#
# Run this with `--max-ply 1` and hand ply 2 onwards to `openings.taper`. The
# two files interlock: every band here is at least as generous as the band
# `openings.taper` gives the same ply, in nodes *and* in MultiPV, so the deep
# pass does not re-queue what the survey already paid for. Loosen a number here
# and nothing breaks; tighten one below `openings.taper` and the deep pass
# quietly buys the same twelve positions twice.
#
# ply  nodes        multipv  margin
0      500000000    36       400
1      600000000    8        70
